  REGION.threads=[
    {id:'camera-questions',title:'Counting cars and keeping journeys are different promises',tag:'Civic life',city:'Frankfort',date:'26 Oct 2026',author:'Ellis Park',profile:'ellis',body:'I read the scope and then the review. The seven-day commitment and fourteen-day configuration are a concrete difference. I am less comfortable with posts claiming we already know who ordered every lookup.',links:[['The Ledger follow-up','#/story/fence-followup'],['The review itself','#/document/review-memo']],comments:[['Nolan Price','The camera hardware alone made me assume it was issuing tickets. I had not read the scope.'],['Ada Wynn','The packet distinguishes the approved purpose from the supplier’s settings. The agenda does not include a promised final vote.','ada'],['Corey Selvin','Safer crossings would be useful. So would a clear answer about deletion. Those can both be true.','corey'],['Tamsin Reed','I still support counting traffic. I do not support the colleague lookup described in the response.']]},
    {id:'commute',title:'Can we put the detour date on the image itself?',tag:'Getting around',city:'Frankfort',date:'25 Oct 2026',author:'Corey Selvin',profile:'corey',body:'The old road graphic is circulating again. Bulletin 4 moves the target to October 30. A screenshot without the date keeps winning the race against the actual update.',links:[['Current bulletin','#/document/road-bulletin']],comments:[['Rowan Pike','We added the version date and bicycle alternative to the revised bulletin. Inspection still comes before reopening.','rowan'],['Amira Cole','My delivery driver had the previous version. A date in the image would help.'],['Ben Arlo','While we are fixing signs, could our bakery deliveries stop being addressed to the shelter meeting?']]},
    {id:'water',title:'That water screenshot is missing its date',tag:'Services',city:'Frankfort',date:'26 Oct 2026',author:'Camila Ortiz',body:'I shared an older notice this morning and have removed it. The current Elm Court notice is planned maintenance on October 28, with possible low pressure. It is not the notice I first posted.',links:[['Current Lockside notice','#/document/lockside-notice']],comments:[['Inez Foster','Thanks for leaving the correction here. I had already forwarded the first picture.'],['Nina Cho','The conservation team’s workshop is separate from service scheduling. The notice has the service-desk contact.','nina-cho'],['Ellis Park','A visible correction is much more useful than an unexplained disappearance.','ellis']]},
    {id:'reading-records',title:'Bringing ordinary paperwork to the reading evening',tag:'Civic life',city:'Frankfort',date:'25 Oct 2026',author:'Dev Malik',profile:'dev',body:'Capitol Commons on Thursday: contracts welcome, but so are garden notices and school-club budgets. We are practicing useful questions, not awarding points for the most intimidating PDF.',links:[['The reading evening','#/story/reading-room']],comments:[['Ada Wynn','I will bring a before-and-after contents page. Exciting to at least three of us.','ada'],['Sam Reed','A document can be readable and still leave something unanswered.','sam'],['Wes Booker','I have a warehouse handover that could use a group intervention.']]},
    {id:'market-tables',title:'The market needs tables; the tables need volunteers',tag:'Local life',city:'Lexington',date:'24 Oct 2026',author:'Amira Cole',body:'November 7 setup starts before the public arrives. If you can help carry tables, please find me at the planning session. We have enough bunting to decorate a modest moon.',links:[['Market preview','#/story/weekend-market']],comments:[['June Ellis','Ceramics stall confirmed. Please do not stack the tables next to the bowls this time.'],['Tessa Brooks','The stall-map proof is ready. I left more room around the repair table.','tessa'],['Nolan Price','I can bring a trolley and a highly specific collection of clamps.']]},
    {id:'learning-hours',title:'Evening learning is also a transport question',tag:'Schools & learning',city:'Lexington',date:'25 Oct 2026',author:'Kai Morgan',profile:'kai',body:'I support the Learning Access idea, but the draft needs to account for the last bus and staff time. I would rather ask those questions now than discover the room is open and nobody can get home.',links:[['Discussion draft','#/document/learning-access']],comments:[['Dana Selvin','Predictable finishing times would help parents plan around it.','dana'],['Mina Holt','A small employer cannot always offer the same shift every week. Flexible sessions would help.'],['Mandy Schmear','Official response: transport is a section in the draft, and rural access is on the listening-session question list.','mandy']]}
  ];

